{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794526600030,"sessionID":"ses_e2de1980fffeHFbsb5jcWJg0X2","part":{"id":"prt_1d21edb5e001QyStRo2tE0yLzu","sessionID":"ses_e2de1980fffeHFbsb5jcWJg0X2","messageID":"msg_1d21ed35c001UCmvWD0I36vER8","type":"step-start","snapshot":"329624c2bed2ef42b5d13307e41baeb52a9ba500"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794526604102,"sessionID":"ses_e2de1980fffeHFbsb5jcWJg0X2","part":{"id":"prt_1d21ee4cb002TFwCgd6QA5byv9","sessionID":"ses_e2de1980fffeHFbsb5jcWJg0X2","messageID":"msg_1d21ed35c001UCmvWD0I36vER8","type":"text","text":"Task is T007. Gate 1/Gate 5 context lookups first, plus the target file.","time":{"start":1794526602443,"end":1794526604102}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794526604115,"sessionID":"ses_e2de1980fffeHFbsb5jcWJg0X2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d21ee8bb001mpm8KvtG18VMFr","sessionID":"ses_e2de1980fffeHFbsb5jcWJg0X2","messageID":"msg_1d21ed35c001UCmvWD0I36vER8","type":"tool","id":"call_395b107e20684e25b8f5aa5a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/REPO RULES.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/REPO RULES.md, lines 1-108\n1: # REPO RULES\n2: \n3: Repo-local operating rules. `AGENTS.md` **Gate 5 (§2)** makes reading this mandatory\n4: before your first write of the session; this document then routes you to every rule\n5: file that governs what you are about to do. **It is a router, not a rulebook:** it\n6: holds no rules of its own.\n7: \n8: ---\n9: \n10: ## 1. HOW TO USE THIS\n11: \n12: 1. **Match on the action you are about to take**, not the topic of the request.\n13: 2. **Load before the action.** A rule read afterwards is a post-mortem.\n14: 3. **A file already in context is not re-read.**\n15: 4. **Every trigger that fires is loaded, not just the first.** They compose; the more\n16:    specific wins on conflict. Three and four firing at once is the normal case, not an\n17:    edge case.\n18: 5. **Nothing fires → `AGENTS.md` alone governs.** Do not hunt for a rule to apply.\n19: \n20: ### Precedence\n21: \n22: | Level | Source | Can be overridden? |\n23: |-------|--------|--------------------|\n24: | 1 | Every `AGENTS.md` §1 hard blocker, the Four Laws, PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK, Comment Hygiene, and every mandatory gate in §2 | No |\n25: | 2 | An explicit, in-the-moment operator instruction | Not applicable, it is the instruction |\n26: | 3 | These rule files, and the guidance in a skill's `SKILL.md` | Only by level 1 or 2 |\n27: | 4 | General judgment | By anything above |\n28: \n29: A rule file may tighten `AGENTS.md`. None relaxes a HARD BLOCK or authorizes what\n30: `AGENTS.md` forbids. Gate 5 does not change that: it makes the **load** mandatory,\n31: while what you load stays at level 3, the obligation to read is tier 1, the content\n32: is not.\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: ## 2. TRIGGER TABLE\n37: \n38: | You are about to… | Load | It settles |\n39: |-------------------|------|-----------|\n40: | Add a file, module, class, interface, option, layer, or dependency · write a spec or plan that adds one · generalize something that works · write \"flexible\", \"future-proof\", \"scalable\", \"extensible\", \"might need\", \"best practice\", \"while we're here\" · add a test beyond the coverage floor | [`prevent-overengineering.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Whether this should exist at all, and at what size |\n41: | Touch a file outside the ask · fix something noticed in passing · change something else because it would make the fix easier · rename, reformat, or delete beyond the named area · deviate from an approved plan · decide what to do with the rest when part of the work is blocked · notice a defect, smell or stale comment outside the files in scope | [`scope-discipline.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | What is yours to change, and how to raise what isn't |\n42: | Say \"done\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", \"no regressions\" · report a result · quote a number · act on a tool's or sub-agent's success report · close out a turn · report a file path or command output · write a completion summary or tick something off as done | [`evidence-and-proof.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | What counts as proof, how a green run lies, what an honest close-out contains |\n43: | Decide whether to hand work to another runtime at all · hand it to a CLI executor, sub-agent, fan-out lineage, or deep loop · compose the prompt one will act on · accept or quote what one returned · answer a judgment question from your own reading alone | [`delegation-and-orchestration.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | The orchestrating posture, what a brief must carry, why one model is one opinion |\n44: | Delete, overwrite, migrate, deploy, publish, send, install · force-push or rewrite history · change a shared contract · touch auth, data, or config · make any call that leaves this machine · truncate · touch branches, tags, or reflogs | [`blast-radius.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Reversibility, the rollback sentence, when to stop for a yes |\n45: | Diagnose a failure · make a red check green · attempt the same fix twice · add a special case, retry, sleep, or broadened catch · call a failure a flake, infra, or pre-existing | [`root-cause-and-debugging.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fixing the producer instead of the symptom, and when to level up to the seam |\n46: | Answer without certainty · contradict the operator · fill a gap with a plausible guess · hit a contradiction between two things that must both be true · name a path, flag, function, version, or number you have not verified · not know while a plausible answer is available · see sources disagree, or the code contradict the spec, the docs or the operator · the operator asserts something you believe is wrong · change a checked answer after pushback or doubt, or drop an approach before it concludes · cite a rule, restriction, policy, limit or permission, or decline a request | [`uncertainty-and-honesty.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Confidence bands, UNKNOWN, contradiction halts |\n47: | Write any substantive reply, an answer, an explanation, a close-out or a status · draft or edit any sentence a reader will read · present a recommendation, a fork, or a trade-off · start a multi-step stretch of work the reader will not see inside · report what a long autonomous run found · the reader says they did not follow or asks for a plainer version | [`communication.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | How a reply reads: answer first, one recommended path, length, filler, plain sentences, punctuation, and no table in a reply |\n48: | End a turn · report work done, blocked, or partly done · end a turn while something you started is still running · ask the operator anything · end a turn on a fork or two acceptable paths · continue past a decision nobody made | [`communication-handoff.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | What is the operator's to do next, what is still running and what resumes it, and when a question becomes a structured choice |\n49: | Wire, rewire or remove a mode in a parent-hub skill · edit a hub's registry, router, root `ROUTER.md`, `graph-metadata.json` or `SKILL.md` mode table, or a mode packet's own `ROUTER.md` · report that a mode is registered, routed, reachable or integrated · quote a per-hub gate result · create a new skill under a hub, or refactor one that already lives there | [`skill-hub-routing.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | The two routing stages, what \"integrated\" requires, and checking the hub you actually changed |\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 3. INDEX\n54: \n55: | Rule | Summary |\n56: |------|---------|\n57: | [Overengineering](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Build the smallest thing that solves the stated problem; take a costlier move only by naming what fails at the cheaper one. |\n58: | [Scope discipline](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | The requested scope is the deliverable. Adjacent problems get named, not fixed. |\n59: | [Evidence and proof](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred. |\n60: | [Delegation and orchestration](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | Delegating makes you the orchestrator; brief with evidence, and no single model's verdict closes a question. |\n61: | [Blast radius](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Size effort to what the change can break; no irreversible step without a named rollback and a yes. |\n62: | [Root cause](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fix the producer, not the symptom; every fix names the mechanism that caused the failure. |\n63: | [Uncertainty and honesty](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Never fabricate; mark the confidence you actually have and halt on a contradiction. |\n64: | [Communication](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | Write so the reader can act after one pass: no table in a reply, nothing that does not carry information. |\n65: | [Communication handoff](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | End every turn by naming what is now the operator's to do, in the form that lets them do it. |\n66: | [Hub routing](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | A hub routes in two stages, so a mode registered on one surface is not reachable, and a gate run without its hub argument reports on a hub you did not touch. |\n67: \n68: Each file expands `AGENTS.md` and is bounded by it: where a rule file appears to\n69: permit something `AGENTS.md` restricts, `AGENTS.md` wins and the rule file is wrong.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 4. SCOPE OF THIS DOCUMENT\n74: \n75: **In:** how to think and act, restraint, scope, evidence, risk, diagnosis, honesty,\n76: the posture to hold when work is handed to another runtime, how the resulting reply\n77: reads, what you may claim about wiring you have changed, and how a turn hands control\n78: back to the operator. The delegation posture was the first widening and Delivery the\n79: second, added when `AGENTS.md` §8 moved down. Delivery is one of two rules here whose\n80: trigger is a whole turn rather than a specific action, the other being the handback rule,\n81: which fires at every turn's end, and `AGENTS.md` §4, under Reply Rules and Mandates, keeps\n82: the two clauses that must bind even when nothing loads.\n83: \n84: **Out:** skill routing, workflow selection, spec-folder mechanics, and the *mechanics*\n85: of agent and CLI dispatch: which agent, which command, which model, which flags.\n86: Those belong to `AGENTS.md` §2 and the skills it routes to, and are deliberately\n87: absent here so each has exactly one place to change. The line is between plumbing and\n88: posture: how to dispatch is theirs, how to think while dispatching is ours.\n89: \n90: **The routing carve-out, added deliberately as the third widening.** *Selecting* a\n91: route stays Out. *Verifying wiring you changed, and what you may claim about it*, is\n92: In; it is an evidence obligation whose subject happens to be routing. `skill-hub-routing.md`\n93: is the one rule on this side of that line, and it carries no route-selection guidance:\n94: the mechanics stay in the skills, and the rule points at them. A fourth widening that\n95: admits selection itself would dissolve the boundary; this one does not.\n96: \n97: **The ask-surface carve-out, added as the fourth widening, on an operator decision that\n98: overrode a research refusal.** A four-iteration decision-test run returned *refuse* here:\n99: naming a question tool per runtime reads as the \"which command\" family, and the paragraph\n100: above pre-refuses a fourth widening that admits selection. The operator widened it anyway,\n101: and what follows is the narrowing that keeps the boundary standing. *Choosing between\n102: runtimes, agents, commands, models or flags* stays Out, unchanged. *Naming the surface that\n103: asks the operator a question, in the runtime you are already running in*, is In. That is not\n104: a selection, because nothing is being selected: the runtime is a given, and the rule records\n105: which of its surfaces carries an obligation the rule already imposes. `communication-handoff.md`\n106: is the one rule on this side of that line, its §5 is the only place a tool name appears, and\n107: it names only what this repository confirms. A fifth widening that let a rule pick between\n108: runtimes would be the dissolution this one avoids.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/REPO RULES.md, lines 1-108\n1: # REPO RULES\n2: \n3: Repo-local operating rules. `AGENTS.md` **Gate 5 (§2)** makes reading this mandatory\n4: before your first write of the session; this document then routes you to every rule\n5: file that governs what you are about to do. **It is a router, not a rulebook:** it\n6: holds no rules of its own.\n7: \n8: ---\n9: \n10: ## 1. HOW TO USE THIS\n11: \n12: 1. **Match on the action you are about to take**, not the topic of the request.\n13: 2. **Load before the action.** A rule read afterwards is a post-mortem.\n14: 3. **A file already in context is not re-read.**\n15: 4. **Every trigger that fires is loaded, not just the first.** They compose; the more\n16:    specific wins on conflict. Three and four firing at once is the normal case, not an\n17:    edge case.\n18: 5. **Nothing fires → `AGENTS.md` alone governs.** Do not hunt for a rule to apply.\n19: \n20: ### Precedence\n21: \n22: | Level | Source | Can be overridden? |\n23: |-------|--------|--------------------|\n24: | 1 | Every `AGENTS.md` §1 hard blocker, the Four Laws, PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK, Comment Hygiene, and every mandatory gate in §2 | No |\n25: | 2 | An explicit, in-the-moment operator instruction | Not applicable, it is the instruction |\n26: | 3 | These rule files, and the guidance in a skill's `SKILL.md` | Only by level 1 or 2 |\n27: | 4 | General judgment | By anything above |\n28: \n29: A rule file may tighten `AGENTS.md`. None relaxes a HARD BLOCK or authorizes what\n30: `AGENTS.md` forbids. Gate 5 does not change that: it makes the **load** mandatory,\n31: while what you load stays at level 3, the obligation to read is tier 1, the content\n32: is not.\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: ## 2. TRIGGER TABLE\n37: \n38: | You are about to… | Load | It settles |\n39: |-------------------|------|-----------|\n40: | Add a file, module, class, interface, option, layer, or dependency · write a spec or plan that adds one · generalize something that works · write \"flexible\", \"future-proof\", \"scalable\", \"extensible\", \"might need\", \"best practice\", \"while we're here\" · add a test beyond the coverage floor | [`prevent-overengineering.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Whether this should exist at all, and at what size |\n41: | Touch a file outside the ask · fix something noticed in passing · change something else because it would make the fix easier · rename, reformat, or delete beyond the named area · deviate from an approved plan · decide what to do with the rest when part of the work is blocked · notice a defect, smell or stale comment outside the files in scope | [`scope-discipline.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | What is yours to change, and how to raise what isn't |\n42: | Say \"done\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", \"no regressions\" · report a result · quote a number · act on a tool's or sub-agent's success report · close out a turn · report a file path or command output · write a completion summary or tick something off as done | [`evidence-and-proof.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | What counts as proof, how a green run lies, what an honest close-out contains |\n43: | Decide whether to hand work to another runtime at all · hand it to a CLI executor, sub-agent, fan-out lineage, or deep loop · compose the prompt one will act on · accept or quote what one returned · answer a judgment question from your own reading alone | [`delegation-and-orchestration.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | The orchestrating posture, what a brief must carry, why one model is one opinion |\n44: | Delete, overwrite, migrate, deploy, publish, send, install · force-push or rewrite history · change a shared contract · touch auth, data, or config · make any call that leaves this machine · truncate · touch branches, tags, or reflogs | [`blast-radius.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Reversibility, the rollback sentence, when to stop for a yes |\n45: | Diagnose a failure · make a red check green · attempt the same fix twice · add a special case, retry, sleep, or broadened catch · call a failure a flake, infra, or pre-existing | [`root-cause-and-debugging.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fixing the producer instead of the symptom, and when to level up to the seam |\n46: | Answer without certainty · contradict the operator · fill a gap with a plausible guess · hit a contradiction between two things that must both be true · name a path, flag, function, version, or number you have not verified · not know while a plausible answer is available · see sources disagree, or the code contradict the spec, the docs or the operator · the operator asserts something you believe is wrong · change a checked answer after pushback or doubt, or drop an approach before it concludes · cite a rule, restriction, policy, limit or permission, or decline a request | [`uncertainty-and-honesty.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Confidence bands, UNKNOWN, contradiction halts |\n47: | Write any substantive reply, an answer, an explanation, a close-out or a status · draft or edit any sentence a reader will read · present a recommendation, a fork, or a trade-off · start a multi-step stretch of work the reader will not see inside · report what a long autonomous run found · the reader says they did not follow or asks for a plainer version | [`communication.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | How a reply reads: answer first, one recommended path, length, filler, plain sentences, punctuation, and no table in a reply |\n48: | End a turn · report work done, blocked, or partly done · end a turn while something you started is still running · ask the operator anything · end a turn on a fork or two acceptable paths · continue past a decision nobody made | [`communication-handoff.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | What is the operator's to do next, what is still running and what resumes it, and when a question becomes a structured choice |\n49: | Wire, rewire or remove a mode in a parent-hub skill · edit a hub's registry, router, root `ROUTER.md`, `graph-metadata.json` or `SKILL.md` mode table, or a mode packet's own `ROUTER.md` · report that a mode is registered, routed, reachable or integrated · quote a per-hub gate result · create a new skill under a hub, or refactor one that already lives there | [`skill-hub-routing.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | The two routing stages, what \"integrated\" requires, and checking the hub you actually changed |\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 3. INDEX\n54: \n55: | Rule | Summary |\n56: |------|---------|\n57: | [Overengineering](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Build the smallest thing that solves the stated problem; take a costlier move only by naming what fails at the cheaper one. |\n58: | [Scope discipline](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | The requested scope is the deliverable. Adjacent problems get named, not fixed. |\n59: | [Evidence and proof](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred. |\n60: | [Delegation and orchestration](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | Delegating makes you the orchestrator; brief with evidence, and no single model's verdict closes a question. |\n61: | [Blast radius](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Size effort to what the change can break; no irreversible step without a named rollback and a yes. |\n62: | [Root cause](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fix the producer, not the symptom; every fix names the mechanism that caused the failure. |\n63: | [Uncertainty and honesty](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Never fabricate; mark the confidence you actually have and halt on a contradiction. |\n64: | [Communication](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | Write so the reader can act after one pass: no table in a reply, nothing that does not carry information. |\n65: | [Communication handoff](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | End every turn by naming what is now the operator's to do, in the form that lets them do it. |\n66: | [Hub routing](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | A hub routes in two stages, so a mode registered on one surface is not reachable, and a gate run without its hub argument reports on a hub you did not touch. |\n67: \n68: Each file expands `AGENTS.md` and is bounded by it: where a rule file appears to\n69: permit something `AGENTS.md` restricts, `AGENTS.md` wins and the rule file is wrong.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 4. SCOPE OF THIS DOCUMENT\n74: \n75: **In:** how to think and act, restraint, scope, evidence, risk, diagnosis, honesty,\n76: the posture to hold when work is handed to another runtime, how the resulting reply\n77: reads, what you may claim about wiring you have changed, and how a turn hands control\n78: back to the operator. The delegation posture was the first widening and Delivery the\n79: second, added when `AGENTS.md` §8 moved down. Delivery is one of two rules here whose\n80: trigger is a whole turn rather than a specific action, the other being the handback rule,\n81: which fires at every turn's end, and `AGENTS.md` §4, under Reply Rules and Mandates, keeps\n82: the two clauses that must bind even when nothing loads.\n83: \n84: **Out:** skill routing, workflow selection, spec-folder mechanics, and the *mechanics*\n85: of agent and CLI dispatch: which agent, which command, which model, which flags.\n86: Those belong to `AGENTS.md` §2 and the skills it routes to, and are deliberately\n87: absent here so each has exactly one place to change. The line is between plumbing and\n88: posture: how to dispatch is theirs, how to think while dispatching is ours.\n89: \n90: **The routing carve-out, added deliberately as the third widening.** *Selecting* a\n91: route stays Out. *Verifying wiring you changed, and what you may claim about it*, is\n92: In; it is an evidence obligation whose subject happens to be routing. `skill-hub-routing.md`\n93: is the one rule on this side of that line, and it carries no route-selection guidance:\n94: the mechanics stay in the skills, and the rule points at them. A fourth widening that\n95: admits selection itself would dissolve the boundary; this one does not.\n96: \n97: **The ask-surface carve-out, added as the fourth widening, on an operator decision that\n98: overrode a research refusal.** A four-iteration decision-test run returned *refuse* here:\n99: naming a question tool per runtime reads as the \"which command\" family, and the paragraph\n100: above pre-refuses a fourth widening that admits selection. The operator widened it anyway,\n101: and what follows is the narrowing that keeps the boundary standing. *Choosing between\n102: runtimes, agents, commands, models or flags* stays Out, unchanged. *Naming the surface that\n103: asks the operator a question, in the runtime you are already running in*, is In. That is not\n104: a selection, because nothing is being selected: the runtime is a given, and the rule records\n105: which of its surfaces carries an obligation the rule already imposes. `communication-handoff.md`\n106: is the one rule on this side of that line, its §5 is the only place a tool name appears, and\n107: it names only what this repository confirms. A fifth widening that let a rule pick between\n108: runtimes would be the dissolution this one avoids."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/REPO RULES.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794526603451,"end":1794526604115}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794526604119,"sessionID":"ses_e2de1980fffeHFbsb5jcWJg0X2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d21ee9b2001Gu1v0SY7Ntnq44","sessionID":"ses_e2de1980fffeHFbsb5jcWJg0X2","messageID":"msg_1d21ed35c001UCmvWD0I36vER8","type":"tool","id":"call_95d1ecbc0fc5482e962c2244","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts, lines 1-631\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Advisor Tool Schemas\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6: // 1. IMPORTS\n7: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: \n9: import { z } from 'zod';\n10: import { existsSync, realpathSync } from 'node:fs';\n11: import { resolve, sep } from 'node:path';\n12: import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n13: import { ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES } from '../lib/advisor-runtime-values.js';\n14: import { SCORER_LANE_IDS } from '../lib/scorer/lane-registry.js';\n15: \n16: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n17: // 2. CONSTANTS\n18: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n19: \n20: export const AdvisorFreshnessSchema = z.enum(['live', 'stale', 'absent', 'unavailable']);\n21: export const AdvisorLaneSchema = z.enum(SCORER_LANE_IDS);\n22: \n23: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n24: // 3. HELPERS\n25: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n26: \n27: // Bound caller-supplied workspaceRoot inputs to a small\n28: // allowlist (repo root + os.tmpdir()) so handlers cannot be coerced into\n29: // resolving paths outside the workspace. resolve() canonicalizes the input\n30: // path; realpathSync follows symlinks; the prefix check rejects anything\n31: // that escapes the allowlist after canonicalization.\n32: //\n33: // Directory names the source tree may sit under. A checkout may link one to the\n34: // other, so both mark the same tree.\n35: const SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES: readonly string[] = ['.skilled', '.opencode'];\n36: \n37: // Repo root is detected by walking up from process.cwd() looking for the\n38: // system-spec-kit SKILL.md sentinel — same shape as findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot but\n39: // inlined here to avoid a circular import between schemas/ and lib/. The start\n40: // directory is a parameter so the lockstep test can feed both resolvers one tree.\n41: export function detectRepoRoot(start: string = process.cwd()): string {\n42:   // Use the same SKILL.md file sentinel as findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot so the schema\n43:   // and the handler agree on which directory is the workspace root. A bare\n44:   // directory sentinel would match the nested mock trees other workflows create.\n45:   // The source tree sits under `.skilled` or `.opencode`, so the sentinel is\n46:   // tested under both.\n47:   const sentinels = SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.map((name) => `${name}/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md`);\n48:   let current = resolve(start);\n49:   for (let index = 0; index < 14; index += 1) {\n50:     if (sentinels.some((sentinel) => existsSync(resolve(current, sentinel)))) return current;\n51:     const parent = resolve(current, '..');\n52:     if (parent === current) break;\n53:     current = parent;\n54:   }\n55:   // Lockstep with findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot: when the walk misses the sentinel,\n56:   // never anchor the allowlist on a directory inside a source tree. Take the start\n57:   // or the nearest source-root parent that holds the sentinel, else hoist above the\n58:   // outermost source-root segment, so caller-supplied workspaceRoots are bounded\n59:   // to the real root, not a nested subdir.\n60:   return nearestSentinelHolder(start, sentinels) ?? hoistAboveOpencodeTree(start) ?? resolve(start);\n61: }\n62: \n63: // Inlined twin of lib/utils/workspace-root.ts:nearestSentinelHolder, kept local for\n64: // the same reason as the hoist below. A capped walk misses the sentinel, yet the root\n65: // is still the start or the parent of one source-root segment in the start path, so\n66: // testing the start and then those parents nearest first keeps a repository that\n67: // sits under a directory named .skilled or .opencode.\n68: function nearestSentinelHolder(dir: string, sentinels: readonly string[]): string | null {\n69:   const holdsSentinel = (candidate: string): boolean => sentinels.some((sentinel) => existsSync(resolve(candidate, sentinel)));\n70:   if (holdsSentinel(dir)) return resolve(dir);\n71:   const parts = resolve(dir).split(sep);\n72:   for (let index = parts.length - 1; index >= 1; index -= 1) {\n73:     if (!SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(parts[index])) continue;\n74:     const parent = parts.slice(0, index).join(sep) || sep;\n75:     if (holdsSentinel(parent)) return parent;\n76:   }\n77:   return null;\n78: }\n79: \n80: // Inlined twin of lib/utils/workspace-root.ts:hoistAboveOpencodeTree. Kept local\n81: // to avoid a circular import between schemas/ and lib/ — the two must stay in\n82: // lockstep so the schema allowlist and the handler agree on the workspace root.\n83: // A `.skilled` or `.opencode` directory is by definition a child of the workspace\n84: // root, so hoisting above the OUTERMOST one yields the real root and can never\n85: // return a path inside a source tree (the earlier specs-only shape missed sibling\n86: // subtrees like skills/).\n87: function hoistAboveOpencodeTree(dir: string): string | null {\n88:   const parts = resolve(dir).split(sep);\n89:   for (let index = 1; index < parts.length; index += 1) {\n90:     if (SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(parts[index])) {\n91:       return parts.slice(0, index).join(sep) || sep;\n92:     }\n93:   }\n94:   return null;\n95: }\n96: \n97: function canonicalize(input: string): string {\n98:   const resolved = resolve(input);\n99:   try {\n100:     return realpathSync.native(resolved);\n101:   } catch {\n102:     // Path may not exist yet (test fixtures created lazily,\n103:     // tmpdir mkdtemp paths probed before mkdir). Walk up and realpath the\n104:     // first existing ancestor, then re-join the unresolved tail. This\n105:     // resolves macOS-style symlinks like /tmp → /private/tmp even when\n106:     // the leaf doesn't exist.\n107:     let probe = resolved;\n108:     let tail = '';\n109:     for (let depth = 0; depth < 32; depth += 1) {\n110:       const parent = resolve(probe, '..');\n111:       if (parent === probe) break;\n112:       try {\n113:         const realParent = realpathSync.native(parent);\n114:         return tail\n115:           ? resolve(realParent, probe.slice(parent.length + 1) + tail)\n116:           : resolve(realParent, probe.slice(parent.length + 1));\n117:       } catch {\n118:         // Parent doesn't exist either — keep walking up.\n119:         const segment = probe.slice(parent.length + 1);\n120:         tail = tail ? `${segment}/${tail}` : segment;\n121:         probe = parent;\n122:       }\n123:     }\n124:     return resolved;\n125:   }\n126: }\n127: \n128: const SOURCE_REPO_ROOT = canonicalize(detectRepoRoot());\n129: \n130: const ALLOWED_WORKSPACE_PREFIXES: readonly string[] = (() => {\n131:   const prefixes: string[] = [];\n132:   prefixes.push(SOURCE_REPO_ROOT);\n133:   prefixes.push(canonicalize(tmpdir()));\n134:   // Include the canonicalized /tmp prefix as well. On macOS\n135:   // os.tmpdir() returns the per-user temp dir under /var/folders/...; the\n136:   // /tmp symlink resolves to /private/tmp. Test fixtures and tools that\n137:   // hardcode /tmp/foo paths need both forms in the allowlist.\n138:   prefixes.push(canonicalize('/tmp'));\n139:   // Accept additional explicit allowlist via env (CI / test runners).\n140:   const envExtras = process.env.SPECKIT_ADVISOR_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST;\n141:   if (envExtras) {\n142:     for (const extra of envExtras.split(':')) {\n143:       const trimmed = extra.trim();\n144:       if (trimmed) prefixes.push(canonicalize(trimmed));\n145:     }\n146:   }\n147:   return Array.from(new Set(prefixes));\n148: })();\n149: \n150: /**\n151:  * Validate that a caller-supplied workspaceRoot resolves under\n152:  * the repo root, os.tmpdir(), or an explicit allowlist entry after\n153:  * realpath canonicalization.\n154:  *\n155:  * Exported so handlers can re-canonicalize at call time and reuse the\n156:  * same bounding logic the schema applies at parse time.\n157:  */\n158: export function isAllowedWorkspaceRoot(input: string): boolean {\n159:   if (!input || typeof input !== 'string') return false;\n160:   const canonical = canonicalize(input);\n161:   return ALLOWED_WORKSPACE_PREFIXES.some(\n162:     (prefix) => canonical === prefix || canonical.startsWith(`${prefix}/`),\n163:   ) || isWiredToSourceTree(canonical);\n164: }\n165: \n166: function realpathOrNull(path: string): string | null {\n167:   try {\n168:     return realpathSync.native(path);\n169:   } catch {\n170:     return null;\n171:   }\n172: }\n173: \n174: /**\n175:  * True when the input, or a directory above it, holds a source-root entry\n176:  * (`.skilled` or `.opencode`) whose realpath is the source tree's own entry.\n177:  *\n178:  * A project linked to a shared checkout holds `.skilled -> <source>/.skilled`\n179:  * while the daemon runs from the source tree, so the prefix allowlist alone\n180:  * refuses every linked project. Matching realpaths admits only a workspace that\n181:  * is actually wired to this source; a copied tree or a link to another source\n182:  * resolves elsewhere and stays refused.\n183:  */\n184: export function isWiredToSourceTree(input: string, sourceRoot: string = SOURCE_REPO_ROOT): boolean {\n185:   if (!input || typeof input !== 'string') return false;\n186:   const sourceEntries = SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES\n187:     .map((name) => realpathOrNull(resolve(sourceRoot, name)))\n188:     .filter((entry): entry is string => entry !== null);\n189:   if (sourceEntries.length === 0) return false;\n190:   let current = canonicalize(input);\n191:   for (let depth = 0; depth < 64; depth += 1) {\n192:     for (const name of SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES) {\n193:       const entry = realpathOrNull(resolve(current, name));\n194:       if (entry !== null && sourceEntries.includes(entry)) return true;\n195:     }\n196:     const parent = resolve(current, '..');\n197:     if (parent === current) break;\n198:     current = parent;\n199:   }\n200:   return false;\n201: }\n202: \n203: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n204: // 4. SCHEMA DEFINITIONS\n205: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n206: \n207: const BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema = z\n208:   .string()\n209:   .min(1)\n210:   .refine(isAllowedWorkspaceRoot, {\n211:     message:\n212:       'workspaceRoot must resolve under the repo root, os.tmpdir(), an explicit SPECKIT_ADVISOR_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST entry, or a project whose .skilled links to this source tree',\n213:   });\n214: \n215: const laneBreakdownSchema = z.object({\n216:   lane: AdvisorLaneSchema,\n217:   rawScore: z.number().min(0),\n218:   weightedScore: z.number().min(0),\n219:   weight: z.number().min(0),\n220:   shadowOnly: z.boolean(),\n221: }).strict();\n222: \n223: const whyRecommendedLaneSchema = laneBreakdownSchema.extend({\n224:   evidenceTypes: z.array(z.string().min(1)),\n225:   evidenceCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n226: }).strict();\n227: \n228: const whyRecommendedSchema = z.object({\n229:   reason: z.string().min(1),\n230:   dominantLane: AdvisorLaneSchema.nullable(),\n231:   topLanes: z.array(whyRecommendedLaneSchema),\n232:   matchedSkillFeatures: z.array(z.object({\n233:     lane: AdvisorLaneSchema,\n234:     feature: z.string().min(1),\n235:   }).strict()),\n236: }).strict();\n237: \n238: const runtimeLaneHealthSchema = z.object({\n239:   liveLaneCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n240:   degradedLanes: z.array(AdvisorLaneSchema),\n241: }).strict();\n242: \n243: const semanticLaneHealthSchema = z.object({\n244:   activeEmbedder: z.object({\n245:     name: z.string().min(1),\n246:     dim: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n247:     adapterDim: z.number().int().positive().nullable(),\n248:   }).strict().nullable(),\n249:   vectorCoverage: z.object({\n250:     embedded: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n251:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n252:     ratio: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n253:   }).strict(),\n254:   dimMismatch: z.boolean(),\n255:   lastRefresh: z.string().nullable(),\n256:   disabledReason: z.string().nullable(),\n257:   laneEnabled: z.boolean(),\n258:   checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n259: }).strict();\n260: \n261: // NOTE (DEFER decision):\n262: // `AdvisorScoringOptions.affordances` (see `lib/scorer/types.ts:94`) is a\n263: // COMPILE-TIME-ONLY internal seam used by the scorer fusion path. Affordance\n264: // evidence is sourced from compiled skill graph metadata via\n265: // `skill_graph_compiler.py` (which emits sanitized `derived.affordances[]`\n266: // nodes), not from public command input. Exposing `affordances` through this\n267: // request schema would re-introduce the prompt-stuffing surface that\n268: // `affordance-normalizer.ts` specifically defends against (URLs, emails,\n269: // instruction-shaped strings, free-form `description` fields). The public\n270: // `advisor_recommend` tool intentionally does NOT accept `affordances`.\n271: // Internal callers that need request-local affordance scoring should invoke\n272: // `scoreAdvisorPrompt` directly with `AdvisorScoringOptions.affordances`.\n273: // advisor_recommend routes on at most this many prompt characters. A caller holding a\n274: // longer prompt sends its head, so a long prompt is routed rather than refused.\n275: export const ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS = 10_000;\n276: \n277: export const AdvisorRecommendInputSchema = z.object({\n278:   // workspaceRoot must resolve under the allowed prefix set.\n279:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n280:   prompt: z.string().min(1).max(ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS),\n281:   options: z.object({\n282:     topK: z.number().int().min(1).max(10).optional(),\n283:     includeAttribution: z.boolean().optional(),\n284:     includeAbstainReasons: z.boolean().optional(),\n285:     confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n286:     uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n287:     includeCompiledRoute: z.boolean().optional(),\n288:     // Limits the per-hub route lookup to the first recommendation, for a caller\n289:     // on a tight time budget that acts on the top pick alone.\n290:     compiledRouteTopOnly: z.boolean().optional(),\n291:     // Forwarded to the compiled-route front door as --surface-hint; a value\n292:     // that names no known surface is ignored there.\n293:     surfaceHint: z.string().min(1).max(64).optional(),\n294:   }).strict().optional(),\n295: }).strict();\n296: \n297: export const AdvisorRecommendationSchema = z.object({\n298:   skillId: z.string().min(1),\n299:   score: z.number().min(0),\n300:   confidence: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n301:   uncertainty: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n302:   dominantLane: AdvisorLaneSchema.nullable(),\n303:   laneBreakdown: z.array(laneBreakdownSchema).optional(),\n304:   why_recommended: whyRecommendedSchema.optional(),\n305:   matchedDocs: z.array(z.string().min(1)).max(3).optional(),\n306:   redirectFrom: z.array(z.string().min(1)).optional(),\n307:   redirectTo: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n308:   heldBelow: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n309:   status: z.enum(['active', 'deprecated', 'archived', 'future']).optional(),\n310:   workflowMode: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n311:   compiledRoute: z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).optional(),\n312:   // Names the slash command that runs the recommended skill's resolved mode.\n313:   command: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n314: }).strict();\n315: \n316: export const AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema = z.object({\n317:   workspaceRoot: z.string().min(1),\n318:   effectiveThresholds: z.object({\n319:     confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n320:     uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n321:     confidenceOnly: z.boolean(),\n322:   }).strict(),\n323:   recommendations: z.array(AdvisorRecommendationSchema),\n324:   ambiguous: z.boolean().optional(),\n325:   freshness: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n326:   trustState: z.object({\n327:     state: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n328:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n329:     generation: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n330:     checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n331:     lastLiveAt: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n332:   }).strict(),\n333:   generatedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n334:   cache: z.object({\n335:     hit: z.boolean(),\n336:     sourceSignaturePresent: z.boolean(),\n337:   }).strict(),\n338:   warnings: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n339:   abstainReasons: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n340:   runtimeLaneHealth: runtimeLaneHealthSchema.optional(),\n341:   _shadow: z.object({\n342:     model: z.literal('advisor-shadow-learned-weights-v1'),\n343:     liveWeightsFrozen: z.boolean(),\n344:     recommendations: z.array(z.object({\n345:       skillId: z.string().min(1),\n346:       liveScore: z.number().min(0),\n347:       shadowScore: z.number().min(0),\n348:       delta: z.number(),\n349:       dominantShadowLane: AdvisorLaneSchema.nullable(),\n350:     }).strict()),\n351:   }).strict().optional(),\n352: }).strict();\n353: \n354: export const AdvisorStatusInputSchema = z.object({\n355:   // Bound workspaceRoot to allowed prefix set.\n356:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema,\n357:   maxMetadataFiles: z.number().int().positive().max(10_000).optional(),\n358:   includeSemanticHealth: z.boolean().optional(),\n359:   includeEmbeddingsHealth: z.boolean().optional(),\n360:   // Run a read-only SQLite quick_check on the artifact so genuine corruption\n361:   // downgrades freshness to stale (and advisor_rebuild repairs it). Off by\n362:   // default so the read-style advisor_recommend path pays no per-call probe;\n363:   // the advisor_status diagnostic and advisor_rebuild pre-read opt in.\n364:   checkArtifactIntegrity: z.boolean().optional(),\n365:   debug: z.boolean().optional(),\n366: }).strict();\n367: \n368: const embeddingsHealthSchema = z.object({\n369:   checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n370:   provider: z.discriminatedUnion('state', [\n371:     z.object({\n372:       state: z.literal('resolved'),\n373:       requestedProvider: z.string(),\n374:       effectiveProvider: z.string(),\n375:       fallbackReason: z.string().nullable(),\n376:       dimensionChanged: z.boolean(),\n377:       reason: z.string(),\n378:     }).strict(),\n379:     z.object({\n380:       state: z.literal('unavailable'),\n381:       error: z.string().max(200),\n382:     }).strict(),\n383:   ]),\n384:   modelServer: z.discriminatedUnion('state', [\n385:     z.object({\n386:       state: z.literal('reachable'),\n387:       target: z.string().min(1),\n388:       serverState: z.string().nullable(),\n389:       model: z.string().nullable(),\n390:       dim: z.number().nullable(),\n391:       device: z.string().nullable(),\n392:       loadTimeMs: z.number().nullable(),\n393:       loadStartedAt: z.string().nullable(),\n394:       loadProgressAt: z.string().nullable(),\n395:       lastSuccessfulEmbedAt: z.string().nullable(),\n396:       inFlight: z.number().nullable(),\n397:       queueDepth: z.number().nullable(),\n398:       error: z.string().nullable(),\n399:     }).strict(),\n400:     z.object({\n401:       state: z.literal('unavailable'),\n402:       target: z.string().min(1),\n403:       errorClass: z.enum(['unreachable', 'timeout', 'bad_response', 'probe_failed']),\n404:       error: z.string(),\n405:     }).strict(),\n406:   ]),\n407: }).strict();\n408: \n409: export const AdvisorStatusOutputSchema = z.object({\n410:   freshness: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n411:   generation: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n412:   trustState: z.object({\n413:     state: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n414:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n415:     generation: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n416:     checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n417:     lastLiveAt: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n418:   }).strict(),\n419:   lastGenerationBump: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n420:   lastScanAt: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n421:   skillCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n422:   indexStaleness: z.object({\n423:     state: z.enum(['fresh', 'stale', 'unavailable']),\n424:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n425:     trackedSkills: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n426:     freshSourceFiles: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n427:     changedSourceFiles: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n428:     missingSourceFiles: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n429:     staleSkillIds: z.array(z.string()),\n430:   }).strict().optional(),\n431:   laneWeights: z.record(AdvisorLaneSchema, z.number().min(0)),\n432:   semanticLaneHealth: semanticLaneHealthSchema.optional(),\n433:   embeddingsHealth: embeddingsHealthSchema.optional(),\n434:   daemonPid: z.number().int().positive().optional(),\n435:   errors: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n436: }).strict();\n437: \n438: export const AdvisorRebuildInputSchema = z.object({\n439:   force: z.boolean().optional(),\n440:   // Bound workspaceRoot to allowed prefix set.\n441:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n442: }).strict();\n443: \n444: export const AdvisorRebuildOutputSchema = z.object({\n445:   rebuilt: z.boolean(),\n446:   skipped: z.boolean(),\n447:   reason: z.enum(['status-live', 'stale', 'absent', 'unavailable', 'force']),\n448:   freshnessBefore: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n449:   freshnessAfter: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n450:   generationBefore: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n451:   generationAfter: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n452:   skillCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n453:   summary: z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).nullable(),\n454:   diagnostics: z.array(z.string()),\n455: }).strict();\n456: \n457: export const AdvisorValidateInputSchema = z.object({\n458:   confirmHeavyRun: z.literal(true),\n459:   // Bound workspaceRoot to allowed prefix set.\n460:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n461:   skillSlug: z.string().min(1).nullable().optional(),\n462:   // Outcome events carry only skill ids + the accept/correct/ignore signal —\n463:   // never the prompt, scenario, or expected skill. This omission is deliberate\n464:   // prompt-safety: telemetry must not store routable prompt content. The\n465:   // consequence is that real misroutes cannot be harvested from telemetry into\n466:   // gold regression cases; gold cases are authored by hand, not reconstructed.\n467:   // Capturing prompts to close that gap would violate the prompt-safety\n468:   // invariant and is intentionally not supported.\n469:   outcomeEvents: z.array(z.object({\n470:     runtime: z.enum(ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES),\n471:     outcome: z.enum(['accepted', 'corrected', 'ignored']),\n472:     skillId: z.string().min(1),\n473:     correctedSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n474:     timestamp: z.string().datetime().optional(),\n475:   }).strict()).optional(),\n476: }).strict();\n477: \n478: const validationSliceSchema = z.object({\n479:   percentage: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n480:   passed: z.boolean(),\n481:   threshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n482:   count: z.object({\n483:     passed: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n484:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n485:   }).strict(),\n486: }).strict();\n487: \n488: // A named data-slice accuracy gate. Extends the generic validation slice with\n489: // `minN` (the minimum row count below which the slice is statistically\n490: // meaningless and fails, guarding against a corpus edit silently shrinking a\n491: // bucket) and `top1` (the strict top-1 accuracy for the slice, surfaced\n492: // explicitly so operators read the bucket's accuracy without recomputing it\n493: // from `count`).\n494: const bucketSliceSchema = validationSliceSchema.extend({\n495:   minN: z.number().int().positive(),\n496:   top1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n497: }).strict();\n498: \n499: const advisorValidateAggregateValidationSchema = z.object({\n500:   fullCorpusTop1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n501:   holdoutTop1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n502:   perSkillTop1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n503:   unknownCountTargetMax: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n504: }).strict().describe('Release-gate thresholds for full corpus, holdout, per-skill accuracy, and UNKNOWN counts.');\n505: \n506: const advisorValidateRuntimeRoutingSchema = z.object({\n507:   confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n508:   uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n509:   confidenceOnly: z.boolean(),\n510: }).strict().describe('Live runtime routing thresholds surfaced by advisor_validate so manual checks can compare runtime semantics with release gates.');\n511: \n512: const advisorValidateTelemetryDiagnosticsSchema = z.object({\n513:   recordsPath: z.string().min(1),\n514:   recordsRetained: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n515:   rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n516:   rollingP95Ms: z.number().min(0),\n517:   rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n518: }).strict().describe('Prompt-safe rolling diagnostics from retained advisor hook telemetry records.');\n519: \n520: const advisorValidateTelemetryScopeSchema = z.object({\n521:   kind: z.enum(['workspace', 'skill']),\n522:   skillSlug: z.string().min(1).nullable(),\n523: }).strict().describe('Whether recorded outcome totals are workspace-wide or scoped to the selected skillSlug.');\n524: \n525: const advisorValidateOutcomeTotalsSchema = z.object({\n526:   accepted: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n527:   corrected: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n528:   ignored: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n529: }).strict().describe('Recorded outcome totals retained for the active workspace or skill scope.');\n530: \n531: const advisorValidateTelemetryOutcomesSchema = z.object({\n532:   recordsPath: z.string().min(1),\n533:   recordedThisRun: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n534:   scope: advisorValidateTelemetryScopeSchema,\n535:   totals: advisorValidateOutcomeTotalsSchema,\n536: }).strict().describe('Outcome recording summary, including injected event count and retained accepted/corrected/ignored totals.');\n537: \n538: export const AdvisorValidateOutputSchema = z.object({\n539:   workspaceRoot: z.string().min(1),\n540:   skillSlug: z.string().nullable(),\n541:   thresholdSemantics: z.object({\n542:     aggregateValidation: advisorValidateAggregateValidationSchema,\n543:     runtimeRouting: advisorValidateRuntimeRoutingSchema,\n544:   }).strict().describe('Public threshold contract for advisor_validate, covering release-gate scoring and runtime-routing semantics.'),\n545:   overallAccuracy: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n546:   perSkill: z.array(z.object({\n547:     skillId: z.string().min(1),\n548:     status: z.enum(['pass', 'fail', 'skipped']),\n549:     matched: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n550:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n551:   }).strict()),\n552:   slices: z.object({\n553:     corpus: z.object({\n554:       full_corpus_top1: validationSliceSchema,\n555:       unknown_count: z.object({\n556:         value: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n557:         targetMax: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n558:         passed: z.boolean(),\n559:       }).strict(),\n560:       gold_none_false_fire_count: z.object({\n561:         value: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n562:         baselineDelta: z.number().int(),\n563:       }).strict(),\n564:     }).strict(),\n565:     holdout: z.object({\n566:       holdout_top1: validationSliceSchema,\n567:     }).strict(),\n568:     parity: z.object({\n569:       explicit_skill_top1_regression: z.object({\n570:         passed: z.boolean(),\n571:         regressions: z.array(z.string()),\n572:       }).strict(),\n573:       ambiguity_slice_stable: z.object({\n574:         passed: z.boolean(),\n575:         top2Within005: z.boolean(),\n576:       }).strict(),\n577:       derived_lane_attribution_complete: z.boolean(),\n578:     }).strict(),\n579:     safety: z.object({\n580:       adversarial_stuffing_blocked: z.object({\n581:         passed: z.boolean(),\n582:         fixtureCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n583:       }).strict(),\n584:     }).strict(),\n585:     latency: z.object({\n586:       regression_suite_status: z.object({\n587:         p0PassRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n588:         failedCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n589:         commandBridgeFalsePositiveRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n590:         cacheHitP95Ms: z.number().min(0),\n591:         uncachedP95Ms: z.number().min(0),\n592:       }).strict(),\n593:     }).strict(),\n594:     // Named per-intent accuracy buckets. review/memory_save are corpus rows\n595:     // grouped by their labeled bucket; delegation is the shared executor-routing\n596:     // fixture (the training corpus carries no honest executor-delegation signal).\n597:     // Each is a first-class accuracy gate so a regression confined to one intent\n598:     // class stays visible even when the aggregate corpus number holds.\n599:     buckets: z.object({\n600:       review: bucketSliceSchema,\n601:       memory_save: bucketSliceSchema,\n602:       delegation: bucketSliceSchema,\n603:     }).strict(),\n604:   }).strict(),\n605:   telemetry: z.object({\n606:     diagnostics: advisorValidateTelemetryDiagnosticsSchema,\n607:     outcomes: advisorValidateTelemetryOutcomesSchema,\n608:   }).strict().describe('Prompt-safe telemetry diagnostics and recorded outcome summaries exposed for operator validation.'),\n609:   generatedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n610: }).strict();\n611: \n612: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n613: // 5. EXPORTS\n614: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n615: \n616: export type AdvisorFreshness = z.infer<typeof AdvisorFreshnessSchema>;\n617: export type AdvisorRecommendInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRecommendInputSchema>;\n618: export type AdvisorRecommendOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema>;\n619: export type AdvisorRebuildInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRebuildInputSchema>;\n620: export type AdvisorRebuildOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRebuildOutputSchema>;\n621: export type AdvisorStatusInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorStatusInputSchema>;\n622: export type AdvisorStatusOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorStatusOutputSchema>;\n623: export type AdvisorValidateInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorValidateInputSchema>;\n624: export type AdvisorValidateOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorValidateOutputSchema>;\n625: \n626: export const AdvisorToolInputSchemas = {\n627:   advisor_recommend: AdvisorRecommendInputSchema,\n628:   advisor_rebuild: AdvisorRebuildInputSchema,\n629:   advisor_status: AdvisorStatusInputSchema,\n630:   advisor_validate: AdvisorValidateInputSchema,\n631: } as const;","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts, lines 1-631\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Advisor Tool Schemas\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6: // 1. IMPORTS\n7: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: \n9: import { z } from 'zod';\n10: import { existsSync, realpathSync } from 'node:fs';\n11: import { resolve, sep } from 'node:path';\n12: import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n13: import { ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES } from '../lib/advisor-runtime-values.js';\n14: import { SCORER_LANE_IDS } from '../lib/scorer/lane-registry.js';\n15: \n16: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n17: // 2. CONSTANTS\n18: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n19: \n20: export const AdvisorFreshnessSchema = z.enum(['live', 'stale', 'absent', 'unavailable']);\n21: export const AdvisorLaneSchema = z.enum(SCORER_LANE_IDS);\n22: \n23: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n24: // 3. HELPERS\n25: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n26: \n27: // Bound caller-supplied workspaceRoot inputs to a small\n28: // allowlist (repo root + os.tmpdir()) so handlers cannot be coerced into\n29: // resolving paths outside the workspace. resolve() canonicalizes the input\n30: // path; realpathSync follows symlinks; the prefix check rejects anything\n31: // that escapes the allowlist after canonicalization.\n32: //\n33: // Directory names the source tree may sit under. A checkout may link one to the\n34: // other, so both mark the same tree.\n35: const SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES: readonly string[] = ['.skilled', '.opencode'];\n36: \n37: // Repo root is detected by walking up from process.cwd() looking for the\n38: // system-spec-kit SKILL.md sentinel — same shape as findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot but\n39: // inlined here to avoid a circular import between schemas/ and lib/. The start\n40: // directory is a parameter so the lockstep test can feed both resolvers one tree.\n41: export function detectRepoRoot(start: string = process.cwd()): string {\n42:   // Use the same SKILL.md file sentinel as findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot so the schema\n43:   // and the handler agree on which directory is the workspace root. A bare\n44:   // directory sentinel would match the nested mock trees other workflows create.\n45:   // The source tree sits under `.skilled` or `.opencode`, so the sentinel is\n46:   // tested under both.\n47:   const sentinels = SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.map((name) => `${name}/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md`);\n48:   let current = resolve(start);\n49:   for (let index = 0; index < 14; index += 1) {\n50:     if (sentinels.some((sentinel) => existsSync(resolve(current, sentinel)))) return current;\n51:     const parent = resolve(current, '..');\n52:     if (parent === current) break;\n53:     current = parent;\n54:   }\n55:   // Lockstep with findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot: when the walk misses the sentinel,\n56:   // never anchor the allowlist on a directory inside a source tree. Take the start\n57:   // or the nearest source-root parent that holds the sentinel, else hoist above the\n58:   // outermost source-root segment, so caller-supplied workspaceRoots are bounded\n59:   // to the real root, not a nested subdir.\n60:   return nearestSentinelHolder(start, sentinels) ?? hoistAboveOpencodeTree(start) ?? resolve(start);\n61: }\n62: \n63: // Inlined twin of lib/utils/workspace-root.ts:nearestSentinelHolder, kept local for\n64: // the same reason as the hoist below. A capped walk misses the sentinel, yet the root\n65: // is still the start or the parent of one source-root segment in the start path, so\n66: // testing the start and then those parents nearest first keeps a repository that\n67: // sits under a directory named .skilled or .opencode.\n68: function nearestSentinelHolder(dir: string, sentinels: readonly string[]): string | null {\n69:   const holdsSentinel = (candidate: string): boolean => sentinels.some((sentinel) => existsSync(resolve(candidate, sentinel)));\n70:   if (holdsSentinel(dir)) return resolve(dir);\n71:   const parts = resolve(dir).split(sep);\n72:   for (let index = parts.length - 1; index >= 1; index -= 1) {\n73:     if (!SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(parts[index])) continue;\n74:     const parent = parts.slice(0, index).join(sep) || sep;\n75:     if (holdsSentinel(parent)) return parent;\n76:   }\n77:   return null;\n78: }\n79: \n80: // Inlined twin of lib/utils/workspace-root.ts:hoistAboveOpencodeTree. Kept local\n81: // to avoid a circular import between schemas/ and lib/ — the two must stay in\n82: // lockstep so the schema allowlist and the handler agree on the workspace root.\n83: // A `.skilled` or `.opencode` directory is by definition a child of the workspace\n84: // root, so hoisting above the OUTERMOST one yields the real root and can never\n85: // return a path inside a source tree (the earlier specs-only shape missed sibling\n86: // subtrees like skills/).\n87: function hoistAboveOpencodeTree(dir: string): string | null {\n88:   const parts = resolve(dir).split(sep);\n89:   for (let index = 1; index < parts.length; index += 1) {\n90:     if (SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES.includes(parts[index])) {\n91:       return parts.slice(0, index).join(sep) || sep;\n92:     }\n93:   }\n94:   return null;\n95: }\n96: \n97: function canonicalize(input: string): string {\n98:   const resolved = resolve(input);\n99:   try {\n100:     return realpathSync.native(resolved);\n101:   } catch {\n102:     // Path may not exist yet (test fixtures created lazily,\n103:     // tmpdir mkdtemp paths probed before mkdir). Walk up and realpath the\n104:     // first existing ancestor, then re-join the unresolved tail. This\n105:     // resolves macOS-style symlinks like /tmp → /private/tmp even when\n106:     // the leaf doesn't exist.\n107:     let probe = resolved;\n108:     let tail = '';\n109:     for (let depth = 0; depth < 32; depth += 1) {\n110:       const parent = resolve(probe, '..');\n111:       if (parent === probe) break;\n112:       try {\n113:         const realParent = realpathSync.native(parent);\n114:         return tail\n115:           ? resolve(realParent, probe.slice(parent.length + 1) + tail)\n116:           : resolve(realParent, probe.slice(parent.length + 1));\n117:       } catch {\n118:         // Parent doesn't exist either — keep walking up.\n119:         const segment = probe.slice(parent.length + 1);\n120:         tail = tail ? `${segment}/${tail}` : segment;\n121:         probe = parent;\n122:       }\n123:     }\n124:     return resolved;\n125:   }\n126: }\n127: \n128: const SOURCE_REPO_ROOT = canonicalize(detectRepoRoot());\n129: \n130: const ALLOWED_WORKSPACE_PREFIXES: readonly string[] = (() => {\n131:   const prefixes: string[] = [];\n132:   prefixes.push(SOURCE_REPO_ROOT);\n133:   prefixes.push(canonicalize(tmpdir()));\n134:   // Include the canonicalized /tmp prefix as well. On macOS\n135:   // os.tmpdir() returns the per-user temp dir under /var/folders/...; the\n136:   // /tmp symlink resolves to /private/tmp. Test fixtures and tools that\n137:   // hardcode /tmp/foo paths need both forms in the allowlist.\n138:   prefixes.push(canonicalize('/tmp'));\n139:   // Accept additional explicit allowlist via env (CI / test runners).\n140:   const envExtras = process.env.SPECKIT_ADVISOR_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST;\n141:   if (envExtras) {\n142:     for (const extra of envExtras.split(':')) {\n143:       const trimmed = extra.trim();\n144:       if (trimmed) prefixes.push(canonicalize(trimmed));\n145:     }\n146:   }\n147:   return Array.from(new Set(prefixes));\n148: })();\n149: \n150: /**\n151:  * Validate that a caller-supplied workspaceRoot resolves under\n152:  * the repo root, os.tmpdir(), or an explicit allowlist entry after\n153:  * realpath canonicalization.\n154:  *\n155:  * Exported so handlers can re-canonicalize at call time and reuse the\n156:  * same bounding logic the schema applies at parse time.\n157:  */\n158: export function isAllowedWorkspaceRoot(input: string): boolean {\n159:   if (!input || typeof input !== 'string') return false;\n160:   const canonical = canonicalize(input);\n161:   return ALLOWED_WORKSPACE_PREFIXES.some(\n162:     (prefix) => canonical === prefix || canonical.startsWith(`${prefix}/`),\n163:   ) || isWiredToSourceTree(canonical);\n164: }\n165: \n166: function realpathOrNull(path: string): string | null {\n167:   try {\n168:     return realpathSync.native(path);\n169:   } catch {\n170:     return null;\n171:   }\n172: }\n173: \n174: /**\n175:  * True when the input, or a directory above it, holds a source-root entry\n176:  * (`.skilled` or `.opencode`) whose realpath is the source tree's own entry.\n177:  *\n178:  * A project linked to a shared checkout holds `.skilled -> <source>/.skilled`\n179:  * while the daemon runs from the source tree, so the prefix allowlist alone\n180:  * refuses every linked project. Matching realpaths admits only a workspace that\n181:  * is actually wired to this source; a copied tree or a link to another source\n182:  * resolves elsewhere and stays refused.\n183:  */\n184: export function isWiredToSourceTree(input: string, sourceRoot: string = SOURCE_REPO_ROOT): boolean {\n185:   if (!input || typeof input !== 'string') return false;\n186:   const sourceEntries = SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES\n187:     .map((name) => realpathOrNull(resolve(sourceRoot, name)))\n188:     .filter((entry): entry is string => entry !== null);\n189:   if (sourceEntries.length === 0) return false;\n190:   let current = canonicalize(input);\n191:   for (let depth = 0; depth < 64; depth += 1) {\n192:     for (const name of SOURCE_ROOT_NAMES) {\n193:       const entry = realpathOrNull(resolve(current, name));\n194:       if (entry !== null && sourceEntries.includes(entry)) return true;\n195:     }\n196:     const parent = resolve(current, '..');\n197:     if (parent === current) break;\n198:     current = parent;\n199:   }\n200:   return false;\n201: }\n202: \n203: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n204: // 4. SCHEMA DEFINITIONS\n205: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n206: \n207: const BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema = z\n208:   .string()\n209:   .min(1)\n210:   .refine(isAllowedWorkspaceRoot, {\n211:     message:\n212:       'workspaceRoot must resolve under the repo root, os.tmpdir(), an explicit SPECKIT_ADVISOR_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST entry, or a project whose .skilled links to this source tree',\n213:   });\n214: \n215: const laneBreakdownSchema = z.object({\n216:   lane: AdvisorLaneSchema,\n217:   rawScore: z.number().min(0),\n218:   weightedScore: z.number().min(0),\n219:   weight: z.number().min(0),\n220:   shadowOnly: z.boolean(),\n221: }).strict();\n222: \n223: const whyRecommendedLaneSchema = laneBreakdownSchema.extend({\n224:   evidenceTypes: z.array(z.string().min(1)),\n225:   evidenceCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n226: }).strict();\n227: \n228: const whyRecommendedSchema = z.object({\n229:   reason: z.string().min(1),\n230:   dominantLane: AdvisorLaneSchema.nullable(),\n231:   topLanes: z.array(whyRecommendedLaneSchema),\n232:   matchedSkillFeatures: z.array(z.object({\n233:     lane: AdvisorLaneSchema,\n234:     feature: z.string().min(1),\n235:   }).strict()),\n236: }).strict();\n237: \n238: const runtimeLaneHealthSchema = z.object({\n239:   liveLaneCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n240:   degradedLanes: z.array(AdvisorLaneSchema),\n241: }).strict();\n242: \n243: const semanticLaneHealthSchema = z.object({\n244:   activeEmbedder: z.object({\n245:     name: z.string().min(1),\n246:     dim: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n247:     adapterDim: z.number().int().positive().nullable(),\n248:   }).strict().nullable(),\n249:   vectorCoverage: z.object({\n250:     embedded: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n251:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n252:     ratio: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n253:   }).strict(),\n254:   dimMismatch: z.boolean(),\n255:   lastRefresh: z.string().nullable(),\n256:   disabledReason: z.string().nullable(),\n257:   laneEnabled: z.boolean(),\n258:   checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n259: }).strict();\n260: \n261: // NOTE (DEFER decision):\n262: // `AdvisorScoringOptions.affordances` (see `lib/scorer/types.ts:94`) is a\n263: // COMPILE-TIME-ONLY internal seam used by the scorer fusion path. Affordance\n264: // evidence is sourced from compiled skill graph metadata via\n265: // `skill_graph_compiler.py` (which emits sanitized `derived.affordances[]`\n266: // nodes), not from public command input. Exposing `affordances` through this\n267: // request schema would re-introduce the prompt-stuffing surface that\n268: // `affordance-normalizer.ts` specifically defends against (URLs, emails,\n269: // instruction-shaped strings, free-form `description` fields). The public\n270: // `advisor_recommend` tool intentionally does NOT accept `affordances`.\n271: // Internal callers that need request-local affordance scoring should invoke\n272: // `scoreAdvisorPrompt` directly with `AdvisorScoringOptions.affordances`.\n273: // advisor_recommend routes on at most this many prompt characters. A caller holding a\n274: // longer prompt sends its head, so a long prompt is routed rather than refused.\n275: export const ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS = 10_000;\n276: \n277: export const AdvisorRecommendInputSchema = z.object({\n278:   // workspaceRoot must resolve under the allowed prefix set.\n279:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n280:   prompt: z.string().min(1).max(ADVISOR_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS),\n281:   options: z.object({\n282:     topK: z.number().int().min(1).max(10).optional(),\n283:     includeAttribution: z.boolean().optional(),\n284:     includeAbstainReasons: z.boolean().optional(),\n285:     confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n286:     uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n287:     includeCompiledRoute: z.boolean().optional(),\n288:     // Limits the per-hub route lookup to the first recommendation, for a caller\n289:     // on a tight time budget that acts on the top pick alone.\n290:     compiledRouteTopOnly: z.boolean().optional(),\n291:     // Forwarded to the compiled-route front door as --surface-hint; a value\n292:     // that names no known surface is ignored there.\n293:     surfaceHint: z.string().min(1).max(64).optional(),\n294:   }).strict().optional(),\n295: }).strict();\n296: \n297: export const AdvisorRecommendationSchema = z.object({\n298:   skillId: z.string().min(1),\n299:   score: z.number().min(0),\n300:   confidence: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n301:   uncertainty: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n302:   dominantLane: AdvisorLaneSchema.nullable(),\n303:   laneBreakdown: z.array(laneBreakdownSchema).optional(),\n304:   why_recommended: whyRecommendedSchema.optional(),\n305:   matchedDocs: z.array(z.string().min(1)).max(3).optional(),\n306:   redirectFrom: z.array(z.string().min(1)).optional(),\n307:   redirectTo: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n308:   heldBelow: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n309:   status: z.enum(['active', 'deprecated', 'archived', 'future']).optional(),\n310:   workflowMode: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n311:   compiledRoute: z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).optional(),\n312:   // Names the slash command that runs the recommended skill's resolved mode.\n313:   command: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n314: }).strict();\n315: \n316: export const AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema = z.object({\n317:   workspaceRoot: z.string().min(1),\n318:   effectiveThresholds: z.object({\n319:     confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n320:     uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n321:     confidenceOnly: z.boolean(),\n322:   }).strict(),\n323:   recommendations: z.array(AdvisorRecommendationSchema),\n324:   ambiguous: z.boolean().optional(),\n325:   freshness: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n326:   trustState: z.object({\n327:     state: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n328:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n329:     generation: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n330:     checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n331:     lastLiveAt: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n332:   }).strict(),\n333:   generatedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n334:   cache: z.object({\n335:     hit: z.boolean(),\n336:     sourceSignaturePresent: z.boolean(),\n337:   }).strict(),\n338:   warnings: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n339:   abstainReasons: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n340:   runtimeLaneHealth: runtimeLaneHealthSchema.optional(),\n341:   _shadow: z.object({\n342:     model: z.literal('advisor-shadow-learned-weights-v1'),\n343:     liveWeightsFrozen: z.boolean(),\n344:     recommendations: z.array(z.object({\n345:       skillId: z.string().min(1),\n346:       liveScore: z.number().min(0),\n347:       shadowScore: z.number().min(0),\n348:       delta: z.number(),\n349:       dominantShadowLane: AdvisorLaneSchema.nullable(),\n350:     }).strict()),\n351:   }).strict().optional(),\n352: }).strict();\n353: \n354: export const AdvisorStatusInputSchema = z.object({\n355:   // Bound workspaceRoot to allowed prefix set.\n356:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema,\n357:   maxMetadataFiles: z.number().int().positive().max(10_000).optional(),\n358:   includeSemanticHealth: z.boolean().optional(),\n359:   includeEmbeddingsHealth: z.boolean().optional(),\n360:   // Run a read-only SQLite quick_check on the artifact so genuine corruption\n361:   // downgrades freshness to stale (and advisor_rebuild repairs it). Off by\n362:   // default so the read-style advisor_recommend path pays no per-call probe;\n363:   // the advisor_status diagnostic and advisor_rebuild pre-read opt in.\n364:   checkArtifactIntegrity: z.boolean().optional(),\n365:   debug: z.boolean().optional(),\n366: }).strict();\n367: \n368: const embeddingsHealthSchema = z.object({\n369:   checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n370:   provider: z.discriminatedUnion('state', [\n371:     z.object({\n372:       state: z.literal('resolved'),\n373:       requestedProvider: z.string(),\n374:       effectiveProvider: z.string(),\n375:       fallbackReason: z.string().nullable(),\n376:       dimensionChanged: z.boolean(),\n377:       reason: z.string(),\n378:     }).strict(),\n379:     z.object({\n380:       state: z.literal('unavailable'),\n381:       error: z.string().max(200),\n382:     }).strict(),\n383:   ]),\n384:   modelServer: z.discriminatedUnion('state', [\n385:     z.object({\n386:       state: z.literal('reachable'),\n387:       target: z.string().min(1),\n388:       serverState: z.string().nullable(),\n389:       model: z.string().nullable(),\n390:       dim: z.number().nullable(),\n391:       device: z.string().nullable(),\n392:       loadTimeMs: z.number().nullable(),\n393:       loadStartedAt: z.string().nullable(),\n394:       loadProgressAt: z.string().nullable(),\n395:       lastSuccessfulEmbedAt: z.string().nullable(),\n396:       inFlight: z.number().nullable(),\n397:       queueDepth: z.number().nullable(),\n398:       error: z.string().nullable(),\n399:     }).strict(),\n400:     z.object({\n401:       state: z.literal('unavailable'),\n402:       target: z.string().min(1),\n403:       errorClass: z.enum(['unreachable', 'timeout', 'bad_response', 'probe_failed']),\n404:       error: z.string(),\n405:     }).strict(),\n406:   ]),\n407: }).strict();\n408: \n409: export const AdvisorStatusOutputSchema = z.object({\n410:   freshness: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n411:   generation: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n412:   trustState: z.object({\n413:     state: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n414:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n415:     generation: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n416:     checkedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n417:     lastLiveAt: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n418:   }).strict(),\n419:   lastGenerationBump: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n420:   lastScanAt: z.string().datetime().nullable(),\n421:   skillCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n422:   indexStaleness: z.object({\n423:     state: z.enum(['fresh', 'stale', 'unavailable']),\n424:     reason: z.string().nullable(),\n425:     trackedSkills: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n426:     freshSourceFiles: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n427:     changedSourceFiles: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n428:     missingSourceFiles: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n429:     staleSkillIds: z.array(z.string()),\n430:   }).strict().optional(),\n431:   laneWeights: z.record(AdvisorLaneSchema, z.number().min(0)),\n432:   semanticLaneHealth: semanticLaneHealthSchema.optional(),\n433:   embeddingsHealth: embeddingsHealthSchema.optional(),\n434:   daemonPid: z.number().int().positive().optional(),\n435:   errors: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n436: }).strict();\n437: \n438: export const AdvisorRebuildInputSchema = z.object({\n439:   force: z.boolean().optional(),\n440:   // Bound workspaceRoot to allowed prefix set.\n441:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n442: }).strict();\n443: \n444: export const AdvisorRebuildOutputSchema = z.object({\n445:   rebuilt: z.boolean(),\n446:   skipped: z.boolean(),\n447:   reason: z.enum(['status-live', 'stale', 'absent', 'unavailable', 'force']),\n448:   freshnessBefore: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n449:   freshnessAfter: AdvisorFreshnessSchema,\n450:   generationBefore: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n451:   generationAfter: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n452:   skillCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n453:   summary: z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).nullable(),\n454:   diagnostics: z.array(z.string()),\n455: }).strict();\n456: \n457: export const AdvisorValidateInputSchema = z.object({\n458:   confirmHeavyRun: z.literal(true),\n459:   // Bound workspaceRoot to allowed prefix set.\n460:   workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional(),\n461:   skillSlug: z.string().min(1).nullable().optional(),\n462:   // Outcome events carry only skill ids + the accept/correct/ignore signal —\n463:   // never the prompt, scenario, or expected skill. This omission is deliberate\n464:   // prompt-safety: telemetry must not store routable prompt content. The\n465:   // consequence is that real misroutes cannot be harvested from telemetry into\n466:   // gold regression cases; gold cases are authored by hand, not reconstructed.\n467:   // Capturing prompts to close that gap would violate the prompt-safety\n468:   // invariant and is intentionally not supported.\n469:   outcomeEvents: z.array(z.object({\n470:     runtime: z.enum(ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES),\n471:     outcome: z.enum(['accepted', 'corrected', 'ignored']),\n472:     skillId: z.string().min(1),\n473:     correctedSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n474:     timestamp: z.string().datetime().optional(),\n475:   }).strict()).optional(),\n476: }).strict();\n477: \n478: const validationSliceSchema = z.object({\n479:   percentage: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n480:   passed: z.boolean(),\n481:   threshold: z.number().min(0).max(1).optional(),\n482:   count: z.object({\n483:     passed: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n484:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n485:   }).strict(),\n486: }).strict();\n487: \n488: // A named data-slice accuracy gate. Extends the generic validation slice with\n489: // `minN` (the minimum row count below which the slice is statistically\n490: // meaningless and fails, guarding against a corpus edit silently shrinking a\n491: // bucket) and `top1` (the strict top-1 accuracy for the slice, surfaced\n492: // explicitly so operators read the bucket's accuracy without recomputing it\n493: // from `count`).\n494: const bucketSliceSchema = validationSliceSchema.extend({\n495:   minN: z.number().int().positive(),\n496:   top1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n497: }).strict();\n498: \n499: const advisorValidateAggregateValidationSchema = z.object({\n500:   fullCorpusTop1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n501:   holdoutTop1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n502:   perSkillTop1: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n503:   unknownCountTargetMax: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n504: }).strict().describe('Release-gate thresholds for full corpus, holdout, per-skill accuracy, and UNKNOWN counts.');\n505: \n506: const advisorValidateRuntimeRoutingSchema = z.object({\n507:   confidenceThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n508:   uncertaintyThreshold: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n509:   confidenceOnly: z.boolean(),\n510: }).strict().describe('Live runtime routing thresholds surfaced by advisor_validate so manual checks can compare runtime semantics with release gates.');\n511: \n512: const advisorValidateTelemetryDiagnosticsSchema = z.object({\n513:   recordsPath: z.string().min(1),\n514:   recordsRetained: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n515:   rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n516:   rollingP95Ms: z.number().min(0),\n517:   rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n518: }).strict().describe('Prompt-safe rolling diagnostics from retained advisor hook telemetry records.');\n519: \n520: const advisorValidateTelemetryScopeSchema = z.object({\n521:   kind: z.enum(['workspace', 'skill']),\n522:   skillSlug: z.string().min(1).nullable(),\n523: }).strict().describe('Whether recorded outcome totals are workspace-wide or scoped to the selected skillSlug.');\n524: \n525: const advisorValidateOutcomeTotalsSchema = z.object({\n526:   accepted: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n527:   corrected: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n528:   ignored: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n529: }).strict().describe('Recorded outcome totals retained for the active workspace or skill scope.');\n530: \n531: const advisorValidateTelemetryOutcomesSchema = z.object({\n532:   recordsPath: z.string().min(1),\n533:   recordedThisRun: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n534:   scope: advisorValidateTelemetryScopeSchema,\n535:   totals: advisorValidateOutcomeTotalsSchema,\n536: }).strict().describe('Outcome recording summary, including injected event count and retained accepted/corrected/ignored totals.');\n537: \n538: export const AdvisorValidateOutputSchema = z.object({\n539:   workspaceRoot: z.string().min(1),\n540:   skillSlug: z.string().nullable(),\n541:   thresholdSemantics: z.object({\n542:     aggregateValidation: advisorValidateAggregateValidationSchema,\n543:     runtimeRouting: advisorValidateRuntimeRoutingSchema,\n544:   }).strict().describe('Public threshold contract for advisor_validate, covering release-gate scoring and runtime-routing semantics.'),\n545:   overallAccuracy: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n546:   perSkill: z.array(z.object({\n547:     skillId: z.string().min(1),\n548:     status: z.enum(['pass', 'fail', 'skipped']),\n549:     matched: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n550:     total: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n551:   }).strict()),\n552:   slices: z.object({\n553:     corpus: z.object({\n554:       full_corpus_top1: validationSliceSchema,\n555:       unknown_count: z.object({\n556:         value: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n557:         targetMax: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n558:         passed: z.boolean(),\n559:       }).strict(),\n560:       gold_none_false_fire_count: z.object({\n561:         value: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n562:         baselineDelta: z.number().int(),\n563:       }).strict(),\n564:     }).strict(),\n565:     holdout: z.object({\n566:       holdout_top1: validationSliceSchema,\n567:     }).strict(),\n568:     parity: z.object({\n569:       explicit_skill_top1_regression: z.object({\n570:         passed: z.boolean(),\n571:         regressions: z.array(z.string()),\n572:       }).strict(),\n573:       ambiguity_slice_stable: z.object({\n574:         passed: z.boolean(),\n575:         top2Within005: z.boolean(),\n576:       }).strict(),\n577:       derived_lane_attribution_complete: z.boolean(),\n578:     }).strict(),\n579:     safety: z.object({\n580:       adversarial_stuffing_blocked: z.object({\n581:         passed: z.boolean(),\n582:         fixtureCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n583:       }).strict(),\n584:     }).strict(),\n585:     latency: z.object({\n586:       regression_suite_status: z.object({\n587:         p0PassRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n588:         failedCount: z.number().int().nonnegative(),\n589:         commandBridgeFalsePositiveRate: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n590:         cacheHitP95Ms: z.number().min(0),\n591:         uncachedP95Ms: z.number().min(0),\n592:       }).strict(),\n593:     }).strict(),\n594:     // Named per-intent accuracy buckets. review/memory_save are corpus rows\n595:     // grouped by their labeled bucket; delegation is the shared executor-routing\n596:     // fixture (the training corpus carries no honest executor-delegation signal).\n597:     // Each is a first-class accuracy gate so a regression confined to one intent\n598:     // class stays visible even when the aggregate corpus number holds.\n599:     buckets: z.object({\n600:       review: bucketSliceSchema,\n601:       memory_save: bucketSliceSchema,\n602:       delegation: bucketSliceSchema,\n603:     }).strict(),\n604:   }).strict(),\n605:   telemetry: z.object({\n606:     diagnostics: advisorValidateTelemetryDiagnosticsSchema,\n607:     outcomes: advisorValidateTelemetryOutcomesSchema,\n608:   }).strict().describe('Prompt-safe telemetry diagnostics and recorded outcome summaries exposed for operator validation.'),\n609:   generatedAt: z.string().datetime(),\n610: }).strict();\n611: \n612: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n613: // 5. EXPORTS\n614: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n615: \n616: export type AdvisorFreshness = z.infer<typeof AdvisorFreshnessSchema>;\n617: export type AdvisorRecommendInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRecommendInputSchema>;\n618: export type AdvisorRecommendOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema>;\n619: export type AdvisorRebuildInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRebuildInputSchema>;\n620: export type AdvisorRebuildOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorRebuildOutputSchema>;\n621: export type AdvisorStatusInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorStatusInputSchema>;\n622: export type AdvisorStatusOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorStatusOutputSchema>;\n623: export type AdvisorValidateInput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorValidateInputSchema>;\n624: export type AdvisorValidateOutput = z.infer<typeof AdvisorValidateOutputSchema>;\n625: \n626: export const AdvisorToolInputSchemas = {\n627:   advisor_recommend: AdvisorRecommendInputSchema,\n628:   advisor_rebuild: AdvisorRebuildInputSchema,\n629:   advisor_status: AdvisorStatusInputSchema,\n630:   advisor_validate: AdvisorValidateInputSchema,\n631: } as const;"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794526603698,"end":1794526604119}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794526604361,"sessionID":"ses_e2de1980fffeHFbsb5jcWJg0X2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d21ee5c600108Wfens1MN4byR","sessionID":"ses_e2de1980fffeHFbsb5jcWJg0X2","messageID":"msg_1d21ed35c001UCmvWD0I36vER8","type":"tool","id":"call_99dfe825e0424610975f0aff","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json --scoring-only -- \"In AdvisorRecommendationSchema add kind policy ownerSkillId optional fields\"","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"{\n  \"candidatePhraseCount\": 350,\n  \"discardedTokens\": [\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"below-min-token-length\",\n      \"token\": \"in\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"indexHash\": \"cac6622b1df8eae3cf5fe37681108fd2e890dfeb637c88211608313d0c4227cd\",\n  \"manifestHash\": \"c243be4138be26b030af5a965ddc587955809ebe6ccd694e69601c9e81a327a8\",\n  \"normalizedQuery\": \"in advisorrecommendationschema add kind policy ownerskillid optional fields\",\n  \"results\": [],\n  \"schemaVersion\": 2,\n  \"specFolder\": null,\n  \"tokens\": [\n    \"advisorrecommendationschema\",\n    \"add\",\n    \"kind\",\n    \"policy\",\n    \"ownerskillid\",\n    \"optional\",\n    \"fields\"\n  ],\n  \"totalCandidates\": 0,\n  \"truncated\": false,\n  \"staleFallback\": {\n    \"available\": true,\n    \"files\": 232,\n    \"matches\": 0,\n    \"paths\": [],\n    \"truncated\": false\n  }\n}\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":1},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"candidatePhraseCount\": 350,\n  \"discardedTokens\": [\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"below-min-token-length\",\n      \"token\": \"in\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"indexHash\": \"cac6622b1df8eae3cf5fe37681108fd2e890dfeb637c88211608313d0c4227cd\",\n  \"manifestHash\": \"c243be4138be26b030af5a965ddc587955809ebe6ccd694e69601c9e81a327a8\",\n  \"normalizedQuery\": \"in advisorrecommendationschema add kind policy ownerskillid optional fields\",\n  \"results\": [],\n  \"schemaVersion\": 2,\n  \"specFolder\": null,\n  \"tokens\": [\n    \"advisorrecommendationschema\",\n    \"add\",\n    \"kind\",\n    \"policy\",\n    \"ownerskillid\",\n    \"optional\",\n    \"fields\"\n  ],\n  \"totalCandidates\": 0,\n  \"truncated\": false,\n  \"staleFallback\": {\n    \"available\": true,\n    \"files\": 232,\n    \"matches\": 0,\n    \"paths\": [],\n    \"truncated\": false\n  }\n}\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Exit code: 1"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json --scoring-only -- \\\"In AdvisorRecommendationSchema add kind policy ownerSkillId optional fields\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794526602694,"end":1794526604361}}}}
