{"type":"text","timestamp":1794526668410,"sessionID":"ses_e2de1980fffeHFbsb5jcWJg0X2","part":{"id":"prt_1d21fd878002TjXbro0TC8ROGC","sessionID":"ses_e2de1980fffeHFbsb5jcWJg0X2","messageID":"msg_1d21fc54d001BkuxPPIvxr5EMA","type":"text","text":"T007 is implemented and its typecheck gate passes. One line of the expected pattern output differs from what the task line predicts.\n\n**File changed** (the only file I touched):\n`/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` — inside `AdvisorRecommendationSchema`, after `command` and before `.strict()`, added three optional fields, with a three-line comment on why they stay optional. `command` and `.strict()` are unchanged. The diff is 6 added lines, no deletions.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n`npm run typecheck` in `ADV`:\n```\n> typecheck\n> ../../system-spec-kit/node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit --composite false -p tsconfig.build.json\n\nTYPECHECK_EXIT=0\n```\nExit 0 and no diagnostics.\n\n`rg -n \"^  (kind|policy|ownerSkillId):\" $SCH`:\n```\n317:  kind: z.enum(['skill', 'command']).optional(),\n318:  policy: z.enum(['run', 'start', 'ask']).optional(),\n319:  ownerSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n527:  kind: z.enum(['workspace', 'skill']),\n```\nThe three new lines print as required. The fourth match is pre-existing: `advisorValidateTelemetryScopeSchema` has a two-space indented `kind` field at line 527, so this pattern cannot print exactly three lines on the current file. Deleting or renaming that field would be outside T007, so I left it. The task's expected output is short by that one line, not the code.\n\n**Not done**\nThe checkbox in `tasks.md` is unticked, as instructed. I ran no test file, because T007 names only the typecheck. The stale-dist warnings in the environment block are pre-existing and untouched.\n\n**Status**: work is edited in the working tree, uncommitted, no git state changed. Residual risk: none known, since the fields are optional and existing output still parses under `.strict()`.\n\nNothing is the operator's to do. The only thing to hand back is the pattern-line discrepancy above, for the coordinator to note against T007's expected output.","time":{"start":1794526664824,"end":1794526668410}}}
